          For RINF XML data sets:
As long as the data provision through XML data sets is allowed, an XML attribute called â€œSetâ€ will be used to link the value of this parameter to the parameter 1.1.1.2.2.1.1 / ECS_SystemType"""@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/uopid
:uopid rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
       rdfs:subPropertyOf :opGenericDataParameter ,
                          <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> ;
       rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
       rdfs:domain :OperationalPoint ;
       rdfs:range xsd:string ;
       :XMLName "UniqueOPID" ;
       :applicable "Y" ;
       :formatNote """CCAAAAAAAAAA
The first part  CC  is the country code in two-letter system of ISO.
The second part is alphanumeric OP code within the MS.
For example, an OP code could be current abbreviation of name used in route books.
In case of borders point, the code is to be selected in the corresponding list in annex 5.1""" ;
       :legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
       :rinfIndex "1.2.0.0.0.2" ;
       :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/BorderPointValidCodeAndCoordinates> ,
                                 <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/BorderPointValidCode> ,
                                 <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/UopidMin> ,
                                 <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/UopidP> ;
       :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "2.2.2" ;
       <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2020-07-29"^^xsd:date ;
       <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2024-01-08"^^xsd:date ,
                                           "2024-09-19"^^xsd:date ,
                                           "2025-03-11"^^xsd:date ;
       <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2019/773/oj> ;
       rdfs:comment "Code composed of country code and alphanumeric operational point code."@en ;
       rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
       rdfs:label "Unique OP ID"@en ;
       rdfs:seeAlso "ISO 3166-1 alpha 2" ;
       <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """Explanation on data presentation: The first two characters represent the country code in two-letter system of ISO.
The second part  AAAAAAAAAA  is maximum 10 Characters String corresponding to OP code within the MS.
'LUAB4' or 'LUAB46TH-G' or 'LUAB4/-_ERT7' are accepted by the validation process.
In case of  borders point , the code is to be selected in the corresponding list in annex 5.1 (this first part  AA  is EU. The second part is  AAAAAAAAAA ). Any OP ID that is not referenced in the annex 5.1 will not be accepted by the validation process.
In case of  domestic borders point , the code will be selected in the corresponding list in annex 5.2 that will be developed later.
Any OP ID that is not referenced in the annex 5.1 will not be accepted by the validation process.
The provided OP ID must be unique within each Member State. The validation has to be made nationally by NRE. The exceptions are  Border point  and  domestic border point  that must be referenced in annex 5.1."""@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/usesGroup555
:usesGroup555 rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
              rdfs:subPropertyOf :tsiCompliantRadioDataParameter ;
              rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
              rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                            owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                          :RunningTrack
                                        )
                          ] ;
              rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
              :applicable "Y/N/NYA" ;
              :dependencyNote "GSM-R and ETCS L2 must be installed for this parameter to be applicable."@en ;
              :eratvIndex "4.13.2.12" ;
              :legalDeadline "12 months after publication of Article 7 Guide for OP tracks"@en ,
                             "16 January 2020"@en ;
              :rinfIndex "1.1.1.3.3.4" ,
                         "1.2.1.1.2.4" ;
              :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/UsesGroup555> ,
                                        <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/UsesGroup555Applicability> ;
              :usedInRCCCalculations "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2020-08-31"^^xsd:date ;
              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2021-09-12"^^xsd:date ,
                                                  "2024-04-18"^^xsd:date ,
                                                  "2025-03-04"^^xsd:date ;
              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> :etcsLevelType ;
              rdfs:comment "Indication if group 555 is used."@en ;
              rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
              rdfs:label "GSM-R use of group 555"@en ;
              <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Sections of EIRENE not covered by references in TSI. GSM-R (parameter 1.1.1.3.3.1) and ETCS L2 (parameter 1.1.1.3.2.1) must be installed for this parameter to be applicable."@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/vNvallowovtrp
:vNvallowovtrp rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
               rdfs:subPropertyOf :etcsNationalValuesDataParameter ;
               rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
               rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                             owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                           :RunningTrack
                                         )
                           ] ;
               rdfs:range [ rdf:type rdfs:Datatype ;
                            owl:onDatatype xsd:unsignedInt ;
                            owl:withRestrictions ( [ xsd:minInclusive "0"^^xsd:unsignedInt
                                                   ]
                                                   [ xsd:maxInclusive "600"^^xsd:unsignedInt
                                                   ]
                                                 )
                          ] ;
               :applicable "Y/N/NYA" ;
               :dependencyNote "A value has to be provided when ETCS is present (a value is provided on 1.1.1.3.2.1)."@en ;
               :formatNote "NNF, with N a decimal number (0 9), NNF must be divisible by 5, so F=(0|5), max. `600`" ;
               :legalDeadline "12 months after publication of Article 7 Guide"@en ;
               :rinfIndex "1.1.1.3.2.16.3" ,
                          "1.2.1.1.1.16.3" ;
               :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/VNvallowovtrp> ,
                                         <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/VNvallowovtrpApplicability> ;
               :tsiOPEAppendixD3Index "1.5.3" ;
               :unitOfMeasure <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloM-PER-HR> ;
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2022-11-07"^^xsd:date ;
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2023-03-14"^^xsd:date ,
                                                   "2024-09-19"^^xsd:date ,
                                                   "2024-12-05"^^xsd:date ;
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> :etcsLevelType ;
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2023/1695/oj> ;
               rdfs:comment """Speed limit allowing the driver to select the  override  function in km/h
According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"""@en ;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
               rdfs:label "V_NVALLOWOVTRP"@en ;
               rdfs:seeAlso "https://www.era.europa.eu/domains/technical-specifications-interoperability/control-command-and-signalling-tsi_en#oe-content-paragraph-1632"^^xsd:anyURI ;
               <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """Format: [NNF], with N a decimal number (0Ã·9), [NNF] must be divisible by 5, so F=(0|5), max. `600`.

See: TSI CCS (Subset-026, Chapter 7. 7.5.1.161)"""@en .


